+# Selected compiled publication source projection
+
+The immutable compiled catalog remains the authority for the complete exact
+three selected profiles, their native policies, final qualification/task/target
+and CPU fit, logical assets and all Core-validated immutable source locations.
+The compiled catalog SHA authenticates HF authority even though the legacy
+GitHub publication file map does not repeat those files.
+
+Publication keeps schema airk.arbiter.publication/1 and exactly three qualified
+model slots. Its assets map contains ONLY files whose approved part primary or
+actual declared backup is an official GitHub release location at the requested
+native release tag. HF-only parts add no GitHub filename. A GitHub backup counts
+regardless of primary origin. Duplicate GitHub filenames must have equal byte
+length/hash; a foreign GitHub tag or Core-rejected origin/backup refuses. The
+public github_part_filenames hook is the same owner used by Service final-source
+slice projection; consumers never guess filenames or promote source URLs.
+
+There is no empty-catalog/count relaxation, no synthetic qualification transfer,
+no changed task/ABI/policy rules and no source or download-availability claim.
+The new Core origin/backup decision and Rust semantic fixtures must pass before
+these consumers mount. Synthetic profiles and URLs in tests are structural
+controls only and are explicitly not public artifact availability evidence.
+
+The existing positive/negative selected-three fixture assertions survive through
+a private test-helper extraction. Additional controls cover three HF-only
+profiles (zero GH assets/full catalog hash), GH backup projection, foreign-tag
+backup refusal, missing selected slot and unapproved backup. Actual production
+fixture emission remains ignored until the three profiles genuinely qualify.
+
+The new projection test can emit the native hypothetical semantic fixture using
+AIRK_ARBITER_PUBLICATION_SOURCE_CASES_OUTPUT. It records HF primary with zero GH
+files and HF primary with a declared GH backup, plus tag/slot refusals. No actual
+fixture emission has occurred during private preparation.
